      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/lisman/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before Lisman existed, the Allen family owned an 8,000‑acre plantation that dominated the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/lisman/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1962, Lisman residents sued the county over voter registration, and in 1966 Martin Luther King Jr. led a rally there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
